# Prevent mixed cached assets in the local cream preview

Status: DONE LOCAL
Milestone: M70 Fresh matching HTML, styles and JavaScript on ordinary navigation
Dependencies: 74_LOCAL_CREAM_MOTION_AND_CURSOR.todo

## Purpose

The owner's screenshot showed current HTML text but the older five-clump status
and ivory cursor. A new document query did not invalidate the unversioned modules.
Fresh-browser checks had missed this delivery problem.

## Tasks

- [x] Inspect the running server and its missing cache-control headers.
- [x] Hash HTML, both stylesheets, the entry module and model into a shared revision.
- [x] Serve versioned CSS/entry URLs and propagate the revision to the model import.
- [x] Disable preview caching and old conditional304responses.
- [x] Restart only the confirmed local preview process on4174.
- [x] Reproduce a real warm-cache old-script load and recover with ordinary navigation.
- [x] Check actual4174revision agreement, extra droplets, pink cursor and motion.
- [x] Reopen the fresh preview without changing the public bakery.

## Acceptance criteria

- A cached old bare module cannot be reused by a new versioned page.
- Both CSS and transitive model imports share the entry revision.
- Future source changes update revision automatically; no manual cache-key edits.
- Existing motion, strawberry material, pointer fallbacks and public files unchanged.

